+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-spec-001"></a>
+
+The clinic also publishes the inverse view of that directory (confirmed 2026-08-21). It lists every specialty the clinic knows, by its stored name, each with the veterinarians holding it `[REQ-SPEC-001]`. Each veterinarian is shown by first name then last name. A veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere on the page, because the page lists specialties rather than the whole roster. Every specialty is shown on one page rather than a page at a time. The page is reachable by its own address alone: no navigation entry and no link from another page leads to it `[REQ-SPEC-001]`.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every specialty is listed by its stored name on one page.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given a specialty one or more veterinarians hold, when the directory is opened, then each of them is listed under it by first name then last name.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on the page.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given any other page of the system, when it is rendered, then no navigation entry and no link on it leads to the specialty directory.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty no veterinarian holds is still listed, with no veterinarian shown against it.
+2. The specialties, and the veterinarians under each, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+3. A clinic that knows no specialty is shown an empty directory rather than a failure.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts) · **ADR:** [ADR: Read-Side View Model for the Specialty Directory](adr/2026-08-21-read-side-view-model-for-the-specialty-directory.md)
+
